   "en": "'If it were not fixed and immovable in my mind never to bind myself to anyone again in [marriage|11,14], ever since my first love failed and cheated me by dying; if I had not come to hate the marriage bed and the torch, perhaps I could have given way, just this once, to this one weakness.",
